{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: re-review the dated active cause at exact clean pushed head 139b54fcfe9a8be641ed1c3eab66985bdeeec925, branch request/dated-active-cause-v2, fulfilling planner's 2906cb7e under promise 60bdd5ee. Artifacts: b230796f internal/workroom, da398d98 cmd/gs, 8f4d3102 docs, 91d82890 AGENTS.md, becd6118 SKILL.md, a11a9535 ui, 2565a04c internal/app.\n\nBEFORE ANYTHING ELSE: I HAD A FALSE ALLOW IN THE HEAD YOU LAST SAW, AND IT WAS YOUR DEFECT REPEATED. I put worldCauseAtOrBefore in the fold with a bare continue at a retired basis -- the same shape as the break you found in staleness(), introduced by me while fixing that one. staleness() inherits the date THROUGH retired artifacts; my walk did not, so it was a strict subset and the receipt boundary admitted what the CLI refused. The implementer authors an interposed artifact and supersedes it after the verdict, and the older pre-verdict cause beneath it disappears. Signer-controllable, no cooperation. An adversarial review found it with a differential fuzz over 400 random histories: 27 divergent cases, one root cause, zero after the fix, and the whole shipped suite green in BOTH directions beforehand.\n\nWHAT ELSE THAT REVIEW FOUND, ALL CLOSED. Neither receipt guard was individually covered -- every receipt test refused through the co-signed path, so neutering the primary check left the package green. The co-signed test was vacuous: its foreign pointer was declared after the receipt, so the plan reached no artifact and the refusal had nothing to do with the rule; it passed with the whole feature deleted. The order test asserted stability but never the value, and taking the latest cause is also order-stable and still wrong. One test's comment described a withdrawal its records never contained. activeRetirements carried a Verdict check that was unreachable. And liveStatement -- the half I missed entirely -- refused an undated superseded world while the artifact beside it was dated, with validateMerge consulting it FIRST, so the change admitted nothing it exists to admit whenever the approval itself carried the flag.\n\nEACH IS NOW PINNED BY NAME UNDER ITS OWN MUTATION. Restoring the continue fails TestAnInterposedRetirementDoesNotHideAnOlderCauseFromTheReceipt. Neutering the primary guard fails TestADirectReceiptRefusesWhenOnlyThePrimaryArtifactWasAlreadyStale. Neutering the co-signed guard fails TestACoSignedMemberOverAlreadyMovedWorldDoesNotWidenTheReceipt, which now carries a positive control. min-to-max in staleness fails the order test with 'world dated at 16, want 14'; the same flip in activeRetirements fails the withdrawal test. I ran every one of those myself.\n\nWHAT I WANT YOU TO ATTACK. The two walks must answer identically for every input, and I have now been wrong about that twice in the same lane. If you can build one history where the published world_superseded_at and the fold's own walk disagree, the design is wrong rather than the code. A differential fuzz is the tool that found it last time.\n\nAGENTS.md IS AMENDED, on hugh's ruling relayed by planner in 2f719949, which lifted the earlier restriction for that paragraph only. Artifact 91d82890 quotes it before and after; the process instruction survives verbatim, scoped to the refusing case.\n\nPERFORMANCE: activeRetirements is built once and passed down rather than rebuilt per receipt and per co-signed basis; the review measured the old shape at roughly twice the fold cost and 64 percent more memory, paid immediately because @10 forces a rebuild.\n\nGATES: gofmt clean over every tracked Go file, go vet clean, go test -count=1 ./... pass, race on cmd/gs 159.390s and internal/workroom 12.243s, internal/docset 50.171s, 83 UI tests pass, git diff --check clean, worktree clean, origin equals the head. ProfileVersion is workroom-fold@10 and artifact b230796f states the deployment order.\n\nCONDITIONS. Confirm the exact head; that the fold walk and the published date agree, by attack rather than inspection; that each named test fails by name under its own mutation; that both receipt guards and both aggregation seams are individually covered; that liveStatement and liveArtifactAsOf share one predicate and both fail closed on zero; that AGENTS.md, SKILL.md, merge.md and architecture.md match the code; and that workroom-fold@10 is warranted. Record Architecture, Security and Simplification.","body":{"branch":"request/dated-active-cause-v2","conditions":"Review exact head 139b54fcfe9a8be641ed1c3eab66985bdeeec925 and artifacts b230796f (internal/workroom), da398d98 (cmd/gs), 8f4d3102 (docs), 91d82890 (AGENTS.md), becd6118 (SKILL.md), a11a9535 (ui), 2565a04c (internal/app) under planner's 2906cb7e. Attack the equivalence of the fold's world walk and the published world_superseded_at -- a differential over random histories is the method that found the last defect; a disagreement is a design fault, not a code fault. Verify by mutation that restoring the continue in worldCauseAtOrBefore fails TestAnInterposedRetirementDoesNotHideAnOlderCauseFromTheReceipt, that neutering each receipt guard fails its own isolating test, and that flipping the earliest-cause comparison in staleness and in activeRetirements fails the order and withdrawal tests respectively. Confirm liveStatement and liveArtifactAsOf share one predicate and both refuse a zero date; that AGENTS.md, SKILL.md, docs/reference/gs/merge.md and docs/reference/architecture.md match the implemented contract; and that workroom-fold@10 is warranted. Record Architecture, Security and Simplification. File approved or changes-requested with gs review naming all seven artifacts. Any head change invalidates review.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}